I started a game as Averin, the lawful dwarven Valkyrie.  I dipped for
Excalibur and found a random luckstone and an amulet of ESP on the way
down, which was helpful since a ton of nymphs came by to steal half my
stuff.  Around this time I'd also killed my Laplace while
hallucinating (which was especially bad since for the first time in
forever I'd found a magic whistle.)  I went through Sokoban and found
a coaligned unicorn on the first level, to whom I threw all my gems.
The treasure zoo was pretty easy, I won an amulet of reflection which
I never really used since no monsters ever hit me with ray attacks.
Descended to the Quest level (DfV-style) and came back up to the
Gnomish Mines since I was only level 12.  Along the way I found a sack
-- my first bag of the game.  I went through Minetown, blessed my
three scrolls of create monster, and *tried* to get lots of monsters
to sacrifice for Mjollnir, but only one (low-level) monster kept being
created every time, so that didn't end up working.  I donated for
protection and found a magic lamp in the lighting shop, but it was
cursed and I didn't have enough potions to make more holy water (I'd
quaffed them all in Sokoban since I didn't have enough room in my
inventory to carry them).

So I descended further into the mines and for whatever unknown reason
the RNG decided to send me...a *master lich* at dlevel 12.  I
panicked.  (I was *still* at xplevel12 by this point.)  I tried
striking him with my two wands of lightning, but they didn't kill
him.  He summoned green dragons and an iron golem.  After hitting a
green dragon once with Excalibur (and noting he was relatively
unharmed, and had stolen half my HP) I used my two magic markers to
write up a scroll of teleportation, only to discover master liches can
apparently teleport TO you.  So I searched my inventory scrupulously
for potions of gain level, things that could be used to alchemize
potions of gain level, scrolls of teleportation, etc., none of which I
had.  I tried writing a scroll of genocide, but well, I'd never seen
one before so it didn't work.  So finally I broke my wand of striking,
which killed me.

Here's the ironic part:
  You were very lucky (7)
  You had extra luck
  Bad luck did not time out for you
  Good luck did not time out for you

I can only assume the RNG wanted me to quit playing NetHack and
actually do something productive this weekend.

